What:		/sys/bus/mipi-dsi/devices/.../fingerprint_hbm
Date:		October 2026
Contact:	zuwwik <zuwwiks@gmail.com>
Description:
		Experimental N11 panel illumination for optical fingerprint capture.
		Reading returns 1 while local HBM is active, otherwise 0. Writing
		1 enables the panel's fixed fingerprint region using the normal
		white 1000-nit command profile and per-panel RGB calibration from
		UEFI SMEM item 498. Writing 0 disables illumination. Writes require
		root. This attribute does not change the desktop backlight value.

		Enabling requires an awake panel, a nonzero backlight, and valid
		calibration. It waits four panel frames before returning. Each
		enable request arms a two-second watchdog. Brightness changes,
		panel disable and driver removal also stop illumination. Failed
		disable commands are retried by the watchdog while the panel runs.

		No daemon enables illumination at boot. This is a development
		interface; libfprint, fprintd and desktop integration are pending.
